NORTHGATE wordmark: text.\n\nNow precise geometry for library layout: I'll create \"Library\" frame: vertical auto-layout, padding 64, gap 64, paper background #F5F3F0? White? Use #F2F0EC paper. Each group: label text + row of variants. Position x=-1720, y=0, width hug? Give fixed width 1500, height hug.\n\nDetailed components:\n\n1. Button variants: create by cloning 1:22 and tweaking: \n   - \"Button / Primary\" — I'll just reference original \"Button\"? To show states in my library, create copies: clone component 1:22? Cloning a COMPONENT creates another component (comp.clone()). I can clone and rename \"Button / Primary\", set on it. But careful: given Button is a COMPONENT (symbol in metadata = component). clone() duplicates as component. Then variants: Primary Hover (#F09D00?), Dark (#17181C bg white text), Dark Hover, Ghost (transparent + white border white text) for dark footer? Footer uses \"Work with us\" — amber on dark pops. Use Primary on footer. Header \"Work with us\" also Primary. So variants: Primary (default, from given), Primary/Hover, Dark, Dark/Hover, Ghost? Keep: Primary, Primary Hover, Dark, Dark Hover. Plus \"Button / Icon\" circle: 48x48 white border with chevron (for prev/next) + hover variant amber.\n   - Buttons need arrow icon inside for CTAs (\"See all listings\", \"Work with us\", \"Contact agent\", \"Learn more\" is link). The given Button has only text. Create \"Button / Primary / Icon\" variant: clone, add arrow instance (rescale to 16x8?) black. Actually simpler: make my button-with-icon as component with auto-layout horizontal gap 10: text + arrow instance. Clone the given Button component (has auto horizontal, padding 0 gap 0 — weird: padding 0 and text 54x21 inside 180x56; alignment probably CENTER CENTER). Set padding to 0, center align, gap 10, add arrow instance recolored black.\n\n2. Nav Item: text 16 Medium ink; hover: amber text + underline? Simple: text color amber for hover. Add small underline bar? Keep color change. Nav items in header could just be texts; but \"navigation\" should be component — create \"Nav / Item\" default+hover; instances in header.\n\n3. Link/Arrow: horizontal auto: text 16 Bold amber? \"Learn more\" links — color: ink with amber arrow, or amber text. I'll do ink bold text + amber arrow (recolor amber), hover all amber. Variants default/hover. Also used on dark CTA: \"Learn more\" on dark → amber text + amber arrow. Create variant \"Link / Arrow / OnDark\".\n\n4. Filter: \"Filter / Default\": white, border #E4E5E8, radius 12, padding 20/24: left text: label small 12 caps muted (\"LOOKING FOR\"?) plus value? Brief text just \"Looking for\". I'll do single row: \"Looking for\" 16 Medium ink + chevron down (muted), space-between, width stretch. \"Filter / Open\": same but amber border + dropdown panel below (options list: \"Any price\", \"$100k–$300k\", \"$300k–$500k\", \"$500k+\") — invented options? It's filter UI content... The brief says design open state yourself; options content is designer's. Slight invention unavoidable for open state. I'll keep generic options. Hmm, is it risky? \"State design\" explicitly includes \"open filter\" — so they expect invented option rows. Fine.\n\n5. Listing Card: vertical, white, border #ECECEF, radius 16, clips content: photo (FILL, 384x270), padding 20: name 20 Bold ink; row: icon+text items (14 Medium body) gap 16: bed \"4 bd\", bath \"2 ba\", area \"1,650 sq ft\". Hover state: shadow + border amber? Create \"Listing Card / Hover\": elevation shadow, translate? Just shadow + slightly amber border. Instances will override photo + texts. Overriding instance text and swapping photo: photo is a nested instance (Photo_Listing_1). To change per card: swap nested instance? Use instanceSwapComponent? For nested instance inside my card instance, I can call `nestedInst.mainComponent = photoComp`? Setting `swapComponent` on nested instance: `inst.swapComponent(newComp)` works on any instance node found inside instance. Yes — find nested instance by name and swapComponent. And override texts via findOne(TEXT name). Plan: inside Listing Card component, embed instance of Photo_Listing_1 named \"Photo\", name texts \"Name\", \"Bd\", \"Ba\", \"Area\". For each usage: create instance, swap Photo to right photo component, set text chars.\n\n6. Detail Item: vertical centered: icon 24 (recolored amber? or ink), value+label: \"4\" bold + \"Bedrooms\" muted? Design: icon 20 amber, text: \"4 Bedrooms\" 16 Medium ink single line. Strip: horizontal auto with dividers between 5 items, padding 24, border radius 12, bg paper.\n\n7. Feature Item: horizontal gap 10: check icon 18 amber + text 16 ink. In 3-col grid.\n\n8. Gallery Thumb: photo instance (e.g., Photo_Modern_House_1) 168x120 radius 8 with 2px transparent border; Selected: border amber 3 + maybe overlay. Default: slight? none.\n\n9. Testimonial Client: horizontal: avatar 56 + col(name 16 Bold ink, \"Client\" 14 muted), padding 12/20, radius 999 chip. Current: white bg + amber ring around avatar / border amber + shadow. Default: transparent bg, opacity? Keep subtle: bg rgba white 0.5? On tint background: default chips plain, current chip white with border.\n\n10. Header component: width 1440 h 88. Logo sub-component? \"Logo\" component (mark + wordmark) reused in header & footer (footer wordmark white). Create \"Logo / Dark\" and \"Logo / Light\" variants. Header: horizontal, padding 0/120, space-between, center: logo left, nav center? Classic: logo left, nav centered absolute? With auto-layout: use SPACE_BETWEEN with 3 groups: [logo][nav][button]. Nav centered-ish. Fine.\n\n11. Footer component: vertical, dark #101015, padding 80/120 48: top row space-between: H2 \"Make your dreams a reality\" white 40 + Button Primary \"Work with us\" with arrow (black icon). divider #26262E. middle row: left col: logo light + social chips row (3 white circles with social logos). right: 3 columns each: title 14 Bold white caps? Title 14 Bold #9A9CA3 caps \"COMPAN