 — from dump, style names like \"Bold\", \"Regular\" exist. Likely also \"Medium\". I'll detect and choose weightStyle = Medium exists ? 'Medium' : 'Regular'.\n\nNow write the code for Call A.\n\nColors:\nconst C = {\n ink:{r:.078,g:.082,b:.098}, // #141519\n body:{r:.345,g:.36,b:.396}, // #585C65\n muted:{r:.55,g:.56,b:.58}, // #8C8F94\n faint:{r:.702,g:.71,b:.725},\n border:{r:.906,g:.91,b:.922}, // #E7E8EB\n line:{r:.15,g:.15,b:.18}, // dark divider\n paper:{r:.977,g:.965,b:.945}, // #F9F6F1\n tint:{r:1,g:.953,b:.871}, // #FFF3DE\n white:{r:1,g:1,b:1},\n amber:{r:1,g:.675,b:.071}, // #FFAC12\n amberD:{r:.91,g:.59,b:.02}, // hover #E89705\n dark:{r:.063,g:.063,b:.078}, // #101014\n darkCard:{r:.11,g:.11,b:.13},\n};\n\nType: H1 56/110%, H2 40/115%, H3 24, body 16/26, small 14.\n\nLetter spacing wordmark: 12% maybe.\n\nHelpers per call (self-contained):\n\n```js\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('5:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nconst dmStyles = (await figma.listAvailableFontsAsync()).filter(f=>f.fontName.family==='DM Sans').map(f=>f.fontName.style);\nconst has = s=>dmStyles.includes(s);\nconst ST = { reg:'Regular', med: has('Medium')?'Medium':'Regular', bold:'Bold' };\nfor (const s of new Set([ST.reg,ST.med,ST.bold])) await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'DM Sans',style:s});\n```\n\nWait Medium could be named \"Medium\" — variable DM Sans typically has named instances: Thin, ExtraLight, Light, Regular, Medium, SemiBold? Actually DM Sans v4 named instances: Thin(100)..Black? Hmm. And styles might include \"9pt-Regular\"? The dump showed \"Bold\" and \"Regular\" plain. Medium likely \"Medium\". OK.\n\nHelper functions:\n\n```js\nfunction T(chars,{size=16,style=ST.reg,color=C.ink,lh,ls,align}={}){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:'DM Sans',style};t.characters=chars;t.fontSize=size;t.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color}];if(lh)t.lineHeight={unit:'PIXELS',value:lh};if(ls)t.letterSpacing={unit:'PERCENT',value:ls};if(align)t.textAlignHorizontal=align;return t;}\nfunction F(name){const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=name;f.fills=[];f.clipsContent=false;return f;}\nfunction AL(f,{dir='VERTICAL',gap=0,pad=[0,0,0,0],align='MIN',cross='MIN',sizing='HUG'}){f.layoutMode=dir;f.itemSpacing=gap;f.paddingTop=pad[0];f.paddingRight=pad[1];f.paddingBottom=pad[2];f.paddingLeft=pad[3];f.primaryAxisAlignItems=align;f.counterAxisAlignItems=cross;if(sizing==='HUG'){f.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO';f.counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO';}return f;}\nasync function inst(id){const c=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);return c.createInstance();}\nfunction solid(node,color){node.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color}];}\nasync function icon(id,color,size){const i=await inst(id);const t=size/Math.max(i.width,i.height);i.rescale(t);i.findAll(n=>n.type==='VECTOR'||n.type==='UNION'||n.type==='BOOLEAN_OPERATION'||n.type==='STAR'||n.type==='ELLIPSE'||n.type==='LINE').forEach(v=>{v.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color}];});return i;}\n```\n\nCareful with rescale: rescale multiplies width/height and rescales children. Instance rescale is allowed. Target: make max dimension = size.\n\nIcon ids:\nIcon_Area 3:4, Arrow_Right 3:3, Bath 3:5, Bed 3:6, Calendar 3:7, Check 3:8, Chevron_Down 3:9, Chevron_Left 3:10, Chevron_Right 3:11, Floors 3:12, Garage 3:13, FB 3:14, IG 3:15, Logo_Mark 3:16, Twitter 3:17, Avatar_Client 3:18, Avatar_Kayley 3:19, Agents_Meeting 3:20, Hero_House 3:21, Listing1 3:22, Listing2 3:23, Listing3 3:24, Listing4 3:25, Listing5 3:26, Modern1 3:27, Modern3 3:28, Modern4 3:29, Modern5 3:30, Modern6 3:31, Modern7 3:32, ModernMain 3:33, Listing6 3:34, Modern2 3:35.\n\nPhotos: inst then resize(w,h).\n\nLibrary creation: I'll place sections in library with headers. Keep tidy: LIB frame VERTICAL gap 56 pad 64, bg white? paper. counterAxisSizing FIXED width 1500? Set f.resize(1500, 100) before AL with sizing AUTO for vertical primary; set counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED'. Fine: after AL, lib.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'; lib.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED'.\n\nEach group: G