{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":42131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"040f6ae7d0400a7aa4ae5b07f7e20bda","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting — Photo_Listing_1 appears to be an interior/conservatory photo, not a house exterior. That's the actual asset, fine. The card looks good. The focused field looks good (amber ring).\n\nNote: the photo in the card fills 400x240 but the image might be distorted — the original photo 3:22 is 278x220; resizing instance to 400x240 — instances of a component with an image fill: resizing scales the frame; the image fill FILL mode will crop... Actually when resizing a frame with image fill, the fill keeps its transform relative — may stretch. It looks fine in screenshot.\n\nNow build 01_Home. This is the big one. Plan sections:\n\n01_Home (1440 wide, white bg):\n1. Header (1440): padding 20/80; logo left; nav center; button right. bottom border. Height ~80.\n2. Hero (1440): padding 96/80; 2-col: left content (label? no — heading 56 bold \"Beautiful homes made for you\", body 18 copy, primary icon button \"See all listings\"), right photo (Photo_Hero_House) cropped to ~640x480 rounded 24. Maybe decorative amber blob behind. Keep clean.\n3. Listings section (paper bg): padding 96/80; heading 40 \"Find your next place to live\" + search button right? Filter bar (card, white, rounded, shadow): 4 filter fields + search button. Then 3x2 grid of 6 listing cards.\n4. Agency intro 1 (white): 2-col: left photo, right text: overline \"WHY NORTHGATE\", heading \"You're in good hands\", copy, \"Learn more\" arrow link.\n5. Agency intro 2 (paper? or white): mirrored: left text, right photo: \"Local experts on every street\", copy, \"Learn more\".\n6. CTA band (dark #101014 rounded 24 inside padding 80): \"Ready to sell your home?\" + copy + \"Learn more\" (amber link). Maybe amber accent shape.\n7. Testimonial (paper): center: big quote mark, quote text 28-32, then 3 client chips in a row (Leo current).\n8. Footer (dark #101014): top: logo + tagline \"Make your dreams a reality\" (big) + \"Work with us\" amber button right; divider; 3 columns links; bottom bar: © + social chips.\n\nHeights: header 80, hero ~640, listings ~1180, intro1 ~560, intro2 ~560, cta ~360, testimonial ~480, footer ~560 → ~4420.\n\n02_Property:\n1. Header (same).\n2. Title bar: padding 40/80: left: h1 \"Modern House\" 40 + address 16 muted; right: price \"$450,000\" 32 bold + \"$280/sq ft\" muted.\n3. Gallery: main photo 1312x560 rounded 24; below: 7 thumbs 132x88 (gap 12 → 7*132+6*12=996) maybe thumbs wider: use FILL row of 7. none selected.\n4. Main 2-col: left (span 8, ~840): Details strip (5 detail items in a row), Description (heading 28 + 3 paragraphs), Features (heading 28 + 15 items in 3-col grid).\n   Right (span 4, ~400, sticky): Agent contact card: avatar 64 + \"Kayley Hall\" bold + \"Agent\" + \"View profile\" link; divider; Name field, Phone field, Email field, Message textarea; \"Contact agent\" primary icon button full width.\n5. Similar listings (paper): heading row: \"Similar listings\" + prev/next circle buttons right; 4 cards in a row.\n6. Footer (same as home).\n\nFooter is repeated → make it a component! Build Footer component once (1440 wide), use instances on both frames. Header too → Header component with instances; prototype link on logo inside instance? Prototype interactions on instances: you can add reactions to instances (they persist). Simpler: header/footer as components; add onClick on the logo instance inside each header instance (interaction on the instance child? You can set reactions on instance children? You can set on the instance root. Better: add reaction to the Logo instance within each Header instance — allowed: instances can have prototype overrides (reactions persist). Actually prototype interactions on nested instances inside an instance — I believe you can set interactions on instance children (\"prototype overrides\"). Yes, Figma supports prototype interaction overrides on nested instances. But safer: set the reaction on the Header instance's logo instance... it's nested two levels (Header instance > Logo instance). Prototype overrides work on any instance descendant. To be safest, I'll make Header a component, and on each Header instance, override the nested Logo instance with an onClick → 01_Home. Alternatively skip making Header a component and build inline frames. But brief says header/footer as reusable components (point 4: \"Design ... the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components\"). So yes components.\n\nFor the prototype reactions:\n- 01_Home: \"See all listings\" button → 02_Property; each of 6 listing cards → 02_Property.\n- 02_Property: header logo → 01_Home; 4 similar cards → 02_Property (self).\nUse reactions: node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, actions:[{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:null,...}]}]. Format: actions: [{ type: \"NODE\", destinationId: \"x:y\", navigation: \"NAVIGATE\", transition: null, preserveScrollPosition: false, overlayRelativePosition: null, resetVideoPosition: false, resetScrollPosition: false, resetComponentVariants: false }]. And overlayModuleBackground? Keep minimal: {trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, actions:[{type:'NODE',destinationId,navigation:'NAVIGATE'}]}. \n\nLet me now write the 01_Home build call. It's big; split into 2 calls: header+hero+listings, then intros+cta+testimonial+footer(+footer component creation).\n\nI'll create the Footer as a component placed in the library, then instances in both frames. Same for Header.\n\nHeader component (1440x80):\n- frame auto-layout HORIZONTAL, padding [0,80], height 80 fixed (primary axis HORIZONTAL: width fixed 1440, height fixed 80? set primaryAxisSizingMode FIXED width 1440, counterAxisSizingMode FIXED 80), align: primary space-between? Use primaryAxisAlignItems 'SPACE_BETWEEN' and counterAxisAlignItems CENTER. Children: Logo instance (Logo / Dark), nav group (4 nav item instances, gap 32), button (Button / Primary / Icon instance, text \"Work with us\").\n- bg white, bottom stroke? strokes on frame apply all sides; use strokeBottomWeight? For frames: strokeBottomWeight supported? There are strokeTopWeight etc. in newer API. Use those: frame.strokes=[border], strokeBottomWeight=1, others 0 (strokeWeight must... set individual weights: strokeTopWeight=0...). I think you can set them after setting strokeWeight. I'll try; if it errors, fallback: no border, just white bg. Actually simpler: add a 1px divider rectangle at bottom inside header (absolute). Or just keep white header over white hero with paper hero bg → separation visible. I'll make hero background paper? Hmm design: header white, hero white, listings paper. Header/hero separation: no border needed; but header over white hero looks floaty — fine, modern. I'll try strokeBottomWeight approach.\n\nNav group: instances of Nav / Item with text Buy/Sell/Rent/About. No current item.\n\nFor heading typography scale:\n- Display/h1 hero: 64 Bold lh 68 ls -2%\n- h2 section: 40 Bold lh 48 ls -1%\n- h3 card title: 20 Bold\n- body: 16 Regular lh 26 body color\n- small: 14 Medium\n- overline: 13 Bold ls 14% amberD uppercase\n\nLet me write call for Header + Footer components first (they're self-contained), then Home part 1, then Home part 2, then Property part 1 + 2, then prototypes, then screenshots.\n\nFooter component (1440 wide, dark):\n- auto-layout VERTICAL, width fixed 1440.\n- Block 1 \"CTA row\": padding [72,80,56,80], HORIZONTAL space-between, cross CENTER: left: tagline \"Make your dreams a reality\" 40 Bold white; right: Button Primary Icon instance \"Work with us\".\n- divider line (1px darkLine) full width: rectangle height 1, fill darkLine, inside padding x80: use a frame with padding [0,80] containing rect w full. Simpler: divider as a child frame with layoutSizingHorizontal FILL height 1 inside a padded wrapper.\n- Block 2 \"links\": padding [56,80], HORIZONTAL, gap: left brand column (Logo / Light instance + small text \"Hand-picked homes, honest advice.\" maybe + social chips row), then 3 columns (Company/Services/Resources) each: col title 13 Bold uppercase darkMuted + 4 links 15 darkText. Layout: brand col width ~400, columns spread. Use SPACE_BETWEEN with a right group of 3 columns gap 80.\n- Block 3 \"bottom\": padding [24,80] HORIZONTAL space-between: left \"© 2026 Northgate Homes. All rights reserved.\" 14 darkMuted; right social chips row (3 instances).\n\nSocial chip instances with swapped logos: swap nested instance: chipInst.findOne(type INSTANCE).swapComponent(twitterComp). The Social / Chip default contains Facebook. For the row: fb as-is, ig swap to 3:15, tw swap to 3:17.\n\nNow Home sections. Photos:\n- Hero: Photo_Hero_House (3:21) 323x220 → crop into 640x520 rounded 24: instance resize to fill cover: set width/height 640x520 directly (image fill FILL will scale/crop? Instance resize stretches the component frame; image fill FILL rescales to cover — when you resize a node with an image fill with scaleMode FILL, the image transform doesn't automatically adjust; actually it stays proportional to node size... Figma keeps the fill relative; visually it may stretch. In the card screenshot, 278x220 → 400x240 looked fine (no visible stretch). OK.\n\nTo crop properly: wrap instance in a clipping frame and size instance larger. For simplicity resize instance to target and accept.\n\n- Agency: Photo_Agents_Meeting (3:20) 330x220 → 640x460.\n- Listing photos 1-6: 3:22..3:26, 3:34.\n\nHome listings data (in order):\n1. Malto House · 4 bd · 2 ba · 1,650 sq ft (Photo_Listing_1)\n2. Birchwood Villa · 4 bd · 2 ba · 1,720 sq ft (Photo_Listing_2)\n3. Cedar Lane House · 4 bd · 2 ba · 1,580 sq ft (Photo_Listing_3)\n4. Harbor View Loft · 4 bd · 2 ba · 1,610 sq ft (Photo_Listing_4)\n5. Maple Court House · 4 bd · 2 ba · 1,690 sq ft (Photo_Listing_5)\n6. Willow Creek Home · 4 bd · 2 ba · 1,640 sq ft (Photo_Listing_6)\n\nTestimonial: quote: \"Kayley and the team found us a home we love in under a month. They knew every street, never pushed us, and we always felt in good hands.\" Clients: Leo Madrigal (current), Owen Brooks, Mia Chen — each \"Client\", Avatar_Client.\n\nFooter columns:\nCompany: About us, Our agents, Careers, Contact\nServices: Buy a home, Sell a home, Rent a home, Property management\nResources: Market reports, Buyer guide, Seller guide, FAQ\n\nHero copy: \"Hand-picked homes, honest advice and a team that knows every street in the neighbourhoods we serve.\"\nIntro1 copy: \"Our agents have helped more than 2,000 families buy, sell and rent. We listen first, explain every step and stay with you until the keys are in your hand.\"\nIntro2 copy: \"We live where we work. From school catchments to the quietest blocks, we can tell you what the listing photos don't.\"\nCTA copy: \"Get a free valuation and a clear plan to sell at the right price, on your timeline.\"\n\nLet me write the Header + Footer call now.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8420bd2b-08e1-4650-9759-ee0744cf2f7f","uuid":"512e7559-2f0c-45dc-9ca8-227092c156b3","timestamp":"2026-11-01T23:51:28.274Z","thinking_duration_ms":57862}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":42131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"040f6ae7d0400a7aa4ae5b07f7e20bda","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_16_a4e137df","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"fileKey":"DevhQt2vYskNKsEjAoLgOj","code":"\nconst lib = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('7:2');\nfor (const s of ['Regular', 'Medium', 'Bold']) await figma.loadFontAsync({ family: 'DM Sans', style: s });\n\nconst C = {\n  ink: { r: 0.078, g: 0.082, b: 0.098 }, body: { r: 0.345, g: 0.36, b: 0.396 }, muted: { r: 0.55, g: 0.56, b: 0.58 },\n  border: { r: 0.898, g: 0.906, b: 0.922 }, paper: { r: 0.977, g: 0.965, b: 0.945 }, tint: { r: 1, g: 0.953, b: 0.871 },\n  white: { r: 1, g: 1, b: 1 }, amber: { r: 1, g: 0.675, b: 0.071 }, amberD: { r: 0.91, g: 0.59, b: 0.02 },\n  dark: { r: 0.063, g: 0.063, b: 0.078 }, darkLine: { r: 0.16, g: 0.16, b: 0.19 },\n  darkText: { r: 0.788, g: 0.792, b: 0.816 }, darkMuted: { r: 0.58, g: 0.585, b: 0.62 },\n};\nfunction T(chars, o = {}) {\n  const t = figma.createText(); t.fontName = { family: 'DM Sans', style: o.style || 'Regular' };\n  t.characters = chars; t.fontSize = o.size || 16; t.fills = [{ type: 'SOLID', color: o.color || C.ink }];\n  if (o.lh) t.lineHeight = { unit: 'PIXELS', value: o.lh };\n  if (o.ls) t.letterSpacing = { unit: 'PERCENT', value: o.ls };\n  return t;\n}\nfunction F(name) { const f = figma.createFrame(); f.name = name; f.fills = []; f.clipsContent = false; return f; }\nfunction AL(f, o = {}) {\n  f.layoutMode = o.dir || 'VERTICAL'; f.itemSpacing = o.gap || 0;\n  const p = o.pad || [0, 0, 0, 0];\n  f.paddingTop = p[0]; f.paddingRight = p[1]; f.paddingBottom = p[2]; f.paddingLeft = p[3];\n  f.primaryAxisAlignItems = o.align || 'MIN'; f.counterAxisAlignItems = o.cross || 'MIN';\n  f.primaryAxisSizingMode = 'AUTO'; f.counterAxisSizingMode = 'AUTO'; return f;\n}\nfunction solid(n, c) { n.fills = [{ type: 'SOLID', color: c }]; }\nconst comp = async name => await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(lib.findOne(n => n.type === 'COMPONENT' && n.name === name).id);\n\n// ---------------- Header ----------------\nconst header = figma.createComponent(); header.name = 'Header';\nlib.appendChild(header); header.x = 0; header.y = lib.height + 200;\nsolid(header, C.white);\nAL(header, { dir: 'HORIZONTAL', pad: [0, 80, 0, 80], align: 'SPACE_BETWEEN', cross: 'CENTER' });\nheader.primaryAxisSizingMode = 'FIXED'; header.counterAxisSizingMode = 'FIXED';\nheader.resize(1440, 88);\nheader.strokes = [{ type: 'SOLID', color: C.border }];\ntry { header.strokeWeight = 1; header.strokeTopWeight = 0; header.strokeLeftWeight = 0; header.strokeRightWeight = 0; header.strokeBottomWeight = 1; } catch (e) {}\n\nconst logoComp = await comp('Logo / Dark');\nheader.appendChild(logoComp.createInstance());\n\nconst nav = F('Nav'); AL(nav, { dir: 'HORIZONTAL', gap: 8, cross: 'CENTER' });\nconst navComp = await comp('Nav / Item');\nfor (const item of ['Buy', 'Sell', 'Rent', 'About']) {\n  const ni = navComp.createInstance();\n  ni.findOne(n => n.type === 'TEXT').characters = item;\n  nav.appendChild(ni);\n}\nheader.appendChild(nav);\n\nconst btnIconComp = await comp('Button / Primary / Icon');\nconst wBtn = btnIconComp.createInstance();\nwBtn.findOne(n => n.type === 'TEXT').characters = 'Work with us';\nheader.appendChild(wBtn);\n\n// ---------------- Footer ----------------\nconst footer = figma.createComponent(); footer.name = 'Footer';\nlib.appendChild(footer); footer.x = 0; footer.y = header.y + header.height + 200;\nsolid(footer, C.dark);\nAL(footer, { dir: 'VERTICAL' });\nfooter.counterAxisSizingMode = 'FIXED'; footer.resize(1440, 100);\n\n// Top: tagline + button\nconst fTop = F('CTA row'); AL(fTop, { dir: 'HORIZONTAL', pad: [72, 80, 56, 80], align: 'SPACE_BETWEEN', cross: 'CENTER' });\nfooter.appendChild(fTop); fTop.layoutSizingHorizontal = 'FILL';\nconst tag = T('Make your dreams a reality', { size: 40, style: 'Bold', color: C.white, ls: -1 });\nfTop.appendChild(tag);\nconst fBtn = btnIconComp.createInstance();\nfBtn.findOne(n => n.type === 'TEXT').characters = 'Work with us';\nfTop.appendChild(fBtn);\n\n// Divider\nconst divWrap = F('divider'); AL(divWrap, { dir: 'VERTICAL', pad: [0, 80, 0, 80] });\nfooter.appendChild(divWrap); divWrap.layoutSizingHorizontal = 'FILL';\nconst div = figma.createRectangle(); div.resize(100, 1); solid(div, C.darkLine);\ndivWrap.appendChild(div); div.layoutSizingHorizontal = 'FILL';\n\n// Middle: brand + link columns\nconst fMid = F('Links'); AL(fMid, { dir: 'HORIZONTAL', pad: [56, 80, 56, 80], align: 'SPACE_BETWEEN', cross: 'MIN' });\nfooter.appendChild(fMid); fMid.layoutSizingHorizontal = 'FILL';\nconst brand = F('Brand'); AL(brand, { dir: 'VERTICAL', gap: 24 });\nconst logoLight = (await comp('Logo / Light')).createInstance();\nbrand.appendChild(logoLight);\nconst blurb = T('Hand-picked homes, honest advice and a team that knows every street in the neighbourhoods we serve.', { size: 15, color: C.darkText, lh: 24 });\nbrand.appendChild(blurb); blurb.layoutSizingHorizontal = 'FIXED'; blurb.resize(320, blurb.height);\nfMid.appendChild(brand);\n\nconst colsWrap = F('Columns'); AL(colsWrap, { dir: 'HORIZONTAL', gap: 88 });\nfMid.appendChild(colsWrap);\nconst cols = [\n  ['Company', ['About us', 'Our agents', 'Careers', 'Contact']],\n  ['Services', ['Buy a home', 'Sell a home', 'Rent a home', 'Property management']],\n  ['Resources', ['Market reports', 'Buyer guide', 'Seller guide', 'FAQ']],\n];\nfor (const [title, links] of cols) {\n  const col = F(title); AL(col, { dir: 'VERTICAL', gap: 14 });\n  col.appendChild(T(title, { size: 13, style: 'Bold', color: C.darkMuted, ls: 12 }));\n  const list = F('list'); AL(list, { dir: 'VERTICAL', gap: 12 });\n  for (const l of links) list.appendChild(T(l, { size: 15, style: 'Medium', color: C.darkText }));\n  col.appendChild(list);\n  colsWrap.appendChild(col);\n}\n\n// Bottom: copyright + socials\nconst fBot = F('Bottom'); AL(fBot, { dir: 'HORIZONTAL', pad: [28, 80, 28, 80], align: 'SPACE_BETWEEN', cross: 'CENTER' });\nfooter.appendChild(fBot); fBot.layoutSizingHorizontal = 'FILL';\nfBot.appendChild(T('© 2026 Northgate Homes. All rights reserved.', { size: 14, color: C.darkMuted }));\nconst soc = F('socials'); AL(soc, { dir: 'HORIZONTAL', gap: 12 });\nconst socComp = await comp('Social / Chip');\nconst fb = socComp.createInstance();\nconst ig = socComp.createInstance();\nig.findOne(n => n.type === 'INSTANCE').swapComponent(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('3:15'));\nconst tw = socComp.createInstance();\ntw.findOne(n => n.type === 'INSTANCE').swapComponent(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('3:17'));\nsoc.appendChild(fb); soc.appendChild(ig); soc.appendChild(tw);\nfBot.appendChild(soc);\n\nreturn JSON.stringify({ header: header.id, footer: footer.id, headerH: header.height, footerH: footer.height });\n","description":"Create Header and Footer master components in library"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8420bd2b-08e1-4650-9759-ee0744cf2f7f","uuid":"c05340e8-cda4-4b9f-bf3e-f0f36110af4e","timestamp":"2026-11-01T23:51:48.165Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_16_a4e137df","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
