{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":44507,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"040f6ae7d0990a7a65500ec4cd124575","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait — the Header/Footer components were appended to `lib` with absolute x/y (lib is an auto-layout frame! appending a child to an auto-layout frame makes it an auto-layout child, so x/y are ignored — header and footer become part of lib's vertical flow, width 1440 fixed while lib is 1560 wide — fine, they'll show as another group. Actually they're auto-layout children now, so lib grew taller. But header/footer don't have the group title/caption treatment — they'll appear directly in lib's flow after the last group with 56px gap. That's acceptable visually. Actually wait — I appended them to lib which has padding 64 and gap 56. So header/footer appear as full-width children — good showcase. But they're not in a \"group\" with a heading. Fine — they're self-evident. Actually let me add heading text above? Skip — acceptable.\n\nHmm, but one issue: header/footer are components inside `lib` auto-layout — their position is managed. That's fine.\n\nNow build 01_Home. Content width 1280 (80px margins).\n\nSections:\n1. Header instance (fixed 1440x88)\n2. Hero (white bg): two columns, left content w≈580, right photo w≈620, gap 40, pad [80,80,96,80]... Let me design: hero pad top 72, bottom 88.\n   - Eyebrow: \"NORTHGATE HOMES · REAL ESTATE AGENCY\"? Adding eyebrow text is optional decoration — allowed (copy beyond fixed list is fine? The brief says must-include items; extra micro-copy like eyebrows is a design decision. I'll add a small eyebrow chip \"REAL ESTATE AGENCY · BROOKLYN, NY\"? Hmm — risk: evaluation is checklist + data accuracy; extra decorative text shouldn't hurt. Keep minimal: a small amber eyebrow \"REAL ESTATE AGENCY\". Safe.\n   - H1 \"Beautiful homes made for you\" 56 Bold, ls -2, lh 64.\n   - Copy: \"Hand-picked homes, honest advice and a team that knows every street in the neighbourhoods we serve.\" 18 Regular body lh 28.\n   - Button instance \"See all listings\" + arrow → link to 02_Property.\n   - Right: photo instance Photo_Hero_House 620x480 r24. Add a floating stat card? Optional decoration; skip or add small badge card with \"2,000+ families\" — nice touch: a small white card overlapping bottom-left of photo: \"2,000+ families helped since 2007\"? That's inventing data (\"since 2007\" is property data...). Skip invented stats; keep clean photo. Maybe add amber accent square behind photo — subtle. Keep simple.\n\n3. Listings section (paper bg #FAF6F1, pad [96,80]): \n   - Heading row: left: eyebrow \"OUR LISTINGS\" + H2 \"Find your next place to live\" (40 Bold). Right: \"See all listings\" arrow link (component instance, change text). Both link to 02.\n   - Filter bar card: white, r16, border, shadow, pad 24: 4 filter fields (instances of 'Field / Filter' w 272 each) + search button amber 56x? A small amber square button with... no search icon available. Use Button/Primary/Icon instance with text \"Search\". The filter component has chevron-down. 4×(272)+gaps 16 = 1168; plus search button... 4×260 = 1040 + 3×16 = 1088 + search 120 → 1224 within 1232 inner width (1280-48). OK: fields w 252 each → 4×252+48=1056, search fills remaining 176. Set fields layoutSizingHorizontal FILL with search fixed. \n   - Grid: 3 cols × 2 rows, gap 32: card w (1280-64)/3 = 405.33 → use FILL. Cards: instances of Listing/Card; override photo (swap inner instance to Photo_Listing_N components), name, meta texts.\n     - Card instance: photoWrap contains an instance of Photo_Listing_1 (3:22). For other cards, find the photo instance inside instance... Instances inside instances: I can swap the nested instance's component? Nested instance inside an instance is accessible via findOne and swapComponent works on nested instances in plugin API (yes, allowed).\n   - Card links: prototype on card → 02_Property.\n\n4. Agency intro 1 (white, pad [96,80]): two columns: left photo (Photo_Agents_Meeting 620x460 r24), right content: eyebrow \"WHY NORTHGATE\", H2 \"You're in good hands\", copy, Learn more arrow link.\n5. Agency intro 2 (paper bg): mirrored: left content, right photo.\n6. Testimonial (white, centered, pad [96,80]): eyebrow \"TESTIMONIALS\", big quote 32 Medium centered lh 44 max-w 900, then clients row: 3 client pill instances centered; Leo Madrigal → swap to 'Testimonial / Client / Current' variant component (just use the Current component instance with Leo name, others default with Owen Brooks / Mia Chen).\n7. CTA band (dark #101014, pad [96,80]): centered: H2 \"Ready to sell your home?\" white 40, copy darkText, Button amber \"Learn more\" + arrow. Maybe amber accent. \n8. Footer instance.\n\nPrototype links on 01_Home: \"See all listings\" button → 02; heading link → 02; each card → 02.\n\n02_Property:\n1. Header instance.\n2. Title bar (white, pad [48,80,32,80]): left: H1 \"Modern House\" 40 Bold; address \"3002 Foster Ave, Brooklyn, NY 11210, USA\" 16 body. Right: price \"$450,000\" 32 Bold; \"$280/sq ft\" 14 muted chip.\n3. Gallery (pad [0,80,64,80]): main photo 1280x560 r20 (Photo_Modern_House_Main), thumbs row below: 7 thumbs 132x88 gap 12? 7×132+6×12=996. Add \"selected: none\" — all default. To hint, could center? Left align. Maybe make thumbs 172x104? 7×172+6×12=1276 ≈1280 nice: thumbs 172 wide, height ~110. Thumb component is 132x88; rescale instances? Instance resize allowed (fill image rescales). resize(172, 110) fine.\n4. Main content (paper bg? sections alternate). Layout: two columns: left main (description, details, features) w 800; right sticky agent card w 416. gap 64. pad [64,80,96,80].\n   - Description: H2 \"Description\" 28 Bold + 3 paragraphs 16 lh 26 body.\n     Para 1: \"A bright, single-storey family home on a quiet tree-lined street, a short walk from Foster Avenue's cafés and the subway.\"\n     Para 2: \"The open-plan kitchen with a large island flows into the living and dining area, with floor-to-ceiling windows onto a private garden. Four bedrooms include a main suite with its own bathroom.\"\n     Para 3: \"Built in 2007 and updated in 2022, the house has a double garage, central air conditioning, new flooring throughout and plenty of built-in storage.\"\n   - Details: H2 \"Details\" + row of 5 detail items (Bed/Bath/Garage/Floors/Calendar): 5 items × ~150 wide. Detail component is hug; row wrap? 5 items in one row, each fixed w 147? Inner content ~800-... main col width: 1280-416-64 = 800. 5×147+4×12=783. OK set each instance fixed w 147? The component is hug — instances can be resized fixed w. Fine, or just hug with natural widths (values differ: \"4\" vs \"2007\"). Use hug + gap 12 — widths vary, acceptable. Actually uniform looks better: set fixed width 147 and fill? simpler: fixed width via resize. I'll resize each to w=147.\n   - Features: H2 \"Features\" + grid 3 cols × 5 rows of Feature/Item instances, gap row 16 col 24.\n   - Agent card (right col): white card r16 border pad 32:\n     - Row: avatar 72 + col(\"Kayley Hall\" 20 Bold, \"Real Estate Agent\"? — invented role text ok? \"View profile\" arrow link small) — must include \"Kayley Hall\" and \"View profile\". Layout: avatar left, name + view profile link under.\n     - Divider\n     - Fields: Name (placeholder \"Your name\"), Phone (\"+1 (555) 000-0000\"? placeholder \"Phone number\"), Email (\"Email address\"), Message textarea \"Hello, I am interested in…\" (exact per brief as placeholder/value).\n     - Button amber full width \"Contact agent\" + arrow.\n   - Use Field/Input instances (the default given Text Field instance + Focus comp?). For form fields on property page: use instances of 'Field / Input / Focus'? No — default state. Use instances of given Text Field (1:25) directly, or create a 'Field / Input' default component... I already have instances. For reuse, use instances of givenTF (Text Field default) — it's a component so reuse OK. But I set labels: Name, Phone, Email. And textarea instance of 'Field / Textarea' component with message placeholder. Contact button = Button/Primary/Icon instance.\n5. Similar listings (white, pad [96,80]): header row: H2 \"Similar listings\" left; right: prev/next circle buttons (chevron-left instance swapped icon, chevron-right). Below: 4 cards w (1280-3×32)/4 = 296 each: FILL. Photo heights: card photo fixed 240 → too tall for 296 wide; resize photoWrap in instance? It's fixed 240 height, FILL horizontal → 296x240 ratio 1.23 vs original 1.67. FILL scaleMode handles crop. OK.\n   - Cards: Malto, Birchwood, Cedar, Harbor (Listings 1-4). Prototype → 02_Property (self).\n6. Footer instance.\n\nNow build 01_Home. Long script — split into two calls: home sections 1-4, then 5-8; then property similarly.\n\nHelper functions duplicated each call. Component IDs:\n- Header 10:2, Footer 10:28, Button/Primary/Icon 7:12, Link/Arrow 7:42, Link/Arrow/OnDark 7:51, Nav 7:34, Listing/Card 9:73, Field/Filter 9:35, Testimonial/Client 9:122, Current 9:127, Feature/Item 9:136, Detail/Item 9:150, Gallery/Thumb 9:114, Button/Circle 7:24, Field/Textarea 9:61, given Text Field 1:25.\nMedia: photos L1..L6: 3:22,3:23,3:24,3:25,3:26,3:34. MH1..7: 3:27,3:35,3:28,3:29,3:30,3:31,3:32. Main 3:33. Hero 3:21. Meeting 3:20. Avatar client 3:18, Kayley 3:19. Icons: area 3:4, arrow 3:3, bath 3:5, bed 3:6, calendar 3:7, check 3:8, chev-down 3:9, chev-left 3:10, chev-right 3:11, floors 3:12, garage 3:13.\n\nListings data:\n1 Malto House 4bd 2ba 1,650 — 3:22\n2 Birchwood Villa 4bd 2ba 1,720 — 3:23\n3 Cedar Lane House 4bd 2ba 1,580 — 3:24\n4 Harbor View Loft 4bd 2ba 1,610 — 3:25\n5 Maple Court House 4bd 2ba 1,690 — 3:26\n6 Willow Creek Home 4bd 2ba 1,640 — 3:34\n\nTestimonial quote: \"Kayley and the team found us a home we love in under a month. They knew every street, never pushed us, and we always felt in good hands.\" — with curly quotes as in data: “...” Include the quote marks.\n\nCopy blocks:\n- Hero copy: \"Hand-picked homes, honest advice and a team that knows every street in the neighbourhoods we serve.\"\n- Intro1 copy: \"Our agents have helped more than 2,000 families buy, sell and rent. We listen first, explain every step and stay with you until the keys are in your hand.\"\n- Intro2 copy: \"We live where we work. From school catchments to the quietest blocks, we can tell you what the listing photos don't.\" (use proper apostrophe ')\n- CTA copy: \"Get a free valuation and a clear plan to sell at the right price, on your timeline.\"\n\nCard builder helper: given cardComp instance, photo swap: find nested instance of photo (name starts 'Photo_'), call swapComponent(target photo comp), then resize to photoWrap size? After swap, new instance size = component size (278x220). Need resize to wrap 400x240. Hmm: photoWrap is 400 wide FILL... In instance, photoWrap width comes from component (400). When card instance is placed in grid with FILL, its width = 405; photoWrap FILL → 405 wide, height fixed 240. The photo child inside photoWrap is NOT auto-layout (photoWrap has no layoutMode) — absolute child; resizing photoWrap doesn't resize photo. So set photo.resize(photoWrap.width, 240). For width I must know final width — set card width fixed per usage: home grid cards fixed 405.33? Make grid columns FILL and after layout... complex. Simpler: give cards FIXED width: home grid card w = 405 (grid: 3×405 + 2×32 = 1279 ≈ 1280, set section inner width 1280, gap 32.5? just use w=406: 3×406+64=1282. Let me use gap 28: 3×408+56=1280. card w 408.)\nSo home cards: fixed width 408; photo resize(408, 240).\nSimilar cards (02): fixed w 296: 4×296+3×32=1280. Photo resize(296,240).\n\nFor overriding meta texts in card instance: findOne TEXT with name 'item' texts... The meta texts are TEXT nodes inside frames named 'item'. In component, ord