ttom? labels on top make fields taller; button height 56 = input 48 + ... put button cross END → aligns bottom with input bottom edge... field height 74 (label 18+8+48). Button 56 at bottom-aligned: baseline ok.)\nFields: instances of 'Field / Filter' — it's a component (cloned givenTF). Set instance FILL horizontal ×4, labels: Looking for, Location, Property Type, Price; placeholders: \"Buy, rent or sell\"? Hmm keep neutral: Looking for → \"Any\", Location → \"Any location\"? Let me pick: Looking for: \"Any\"; Location: \"All locations\"; Property Type: \"Any type\"; Price: \"Any price\". Search button: Button/Primary/Icon instance text \"Search\" — icon arrow right ok.\n\nCards grid: vertical rows of 3, gap 28/32.\n\nCard creation helper in code:\nasync function listingCard(data) {\n  const c = cardComp.createInstance();\n  c.counterAxisSizingMode... instance resize: set fixed width 408: c.resize(408, c.height)? For instance with counterAxisSizingMode FIXED in component, resize allowed. photoWrap FILL → auto width. photo resize(408,240) after.\n  swap photo, texts. Return.\n}\nFor home, photo h 240 fine (408x240 ratio 1.7).\n\nPrototype reactions later.\n\nLet me write call A now. Keep code lean. Note apostrophes in strings — use Unicode ' where needed (copy says \"don't\" with straight? data text: \"don't\" typographic in brief (don't). I'll use ' (U+2019) to match the brief's typographic style. The brief text uses '’'. In DATA: \"what the listing photos don't.\" — I'll use ’. Similarly \"You're in good hands\" with ’, \"Foster Avenue's cafés\" with ’, \"Hello, I am interested in…\" ellipsis ….\n\nNote heading \"You're in good hands\" with curly apostrophe.\n\nGo.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8420bd2b-08e1-4650-9759-ee0744cf2f7f","uuid":"26a3f674-f019-4e3d-b26e-9c6f603a3ce6","timestamp":"2026-11-01T23:53:31.684Z","thinking_duration_ms":94448}
